\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ/Slowing Yen's -4: Some Anticipate Volatile Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1998\par 20:37\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  As a result, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market could be quite volatile, as participants weigh the likelihood of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commitment to reform, recovery efforts of Indonesia and policy statements from the G-7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  "People are looking at very volatile conditions after several sessions of being comatose," said Lisa Finstrom, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with Salomon Smith Barney in New York. \par \par \uc2  Some believe that Thursday's action may represent a watershed, reversing the dollar's more than three-year march higher against the yen, from around Y80.00. "They're not going to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  around Y130," said IDEA's Durrant. "They won't allow the dollar to climb back up." \par \par \uc2  Not everyone agrees. In a faxed note, Avinash Persaud, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with J.P. Morgan in London, asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could sustainably lift the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The answer must be no," he wrote. \par \par \uc2  Although the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  as recently as the end of last year, the Fed last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy yen for dollars in February 1992 when the dollar was at Y127.50. On Feb. 17, 1992 the Fed bought yen in the Tokyo trading session, as U.S. markets were closed for President's Day. \par \par \uc2  That move effectively kick-started a steady, three-year rise in the yen that only ended when joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was again initiated midway through 1995, this time to buy dollars for yen at around Y82.00. \par \par \uc2  A series of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred in 1995, involving central banks from the U.S., Japan, Germany and other European governments. They were apparently undertaken to reassure markets that the Clinton administration did not want to use the weaker dollar as a trade weapon in an ongoing dispute with Japan. \par \par \uc2  By Michael Casey, Kenji Hall and Paul Podolsky \par \par \uc2  e-mail: Paul.Podolsky@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  09-04-98 \par \par \uc2  1837GMT \par \par \uc2  1148 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010917du49002qi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
