\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ/Slowing Yen's Fall -3: Cool Reaction To Tax Cuts \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1998\par 19:57\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  "I wouldn't look for that much lasting impact out of this," said Andrew Hodge, vice president, financial strategist at Bank Brussels Lambert. The BOJ action will merely result in a slowing of the yen's decline, he said. \par \par \uc2  For Thursday, however, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should take pressure off the yen, as the dollar selling for yen cleared out long dollar positions, or bets the dollar will rise against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Bank Brussels Lambert sold $10 million in around 10 seconds when bond traders on their proprietary trading desk got wind of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Hodge said. "We just managed to get out by the skin of our teeth," \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's timing was well chosen. \par \par \uc2  After a negative reaction to Hashimoto's package, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to send a message and in a way that would maximize the effectiveness of the move. \par \par \uc2  "There are only a couple of times when Japan is in (the market) and the rest of the world is out," said David Durrant, a global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at IDEA in New York. "Easter is one of those times." \par \par \uc2  Some saw the move as a tacit admission by the Japanese that the tax cut announcement - which the U.S. had advocated - failed to achieve its intended purpose. \par \par \uc2  Frustration, in other words, was likely a factor in the BOJ decision, which drove home the government's commitment to reform, said Bob Lynch, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Banque Paribas in New York. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese "have to make this statement, to show they are trying to do something, that they've introduced tax cuts, that they're \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen," Lynch said. "They're saying: 'Stick with us, we are trying to do the best we can.'" \par \par \uc2  To be sure, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't in itself alter \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unattractive fundamentals, which the yen's price will ultimately reflect, said Lynch. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  09-04-98 \par \par \uc2  1757GMT \par \par \uc2  1148 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010917du49002qd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
