\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Crisis At A Glance: Fed Sells Dlrs On Behalf Of BOJ \b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1998\par 21:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  -- The Federal Reserve Bank of New York, acting on behalf of the Bank of Japan, sold yen for dollars at around 1320 GMT. [R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Around 1813 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y130.38, up from its low of Y129.54 after the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but down from Y131.33 late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  -- Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin Thursday welcomed action taken by Japanese authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the yen. [R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- Rubin and his senior aides have been laying a rhetorical foundation for dollar sales against the Japanese yen for nearly a year, but concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has some big question marks hanging over it. [R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading Thursday will likely slow - but not reverse - the dollar's rise against the yen, according to market participants. [R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- Japanese government bond futures prices ended higher Thursday on the London International Financial Futures and Options Exchange (Liffe) after the Federal Reserve Bank of New York acting on behalf of the Bank of Japan sold dollars for yen. [R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga Thursday said Japan took 'decisive action' in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on the same day to support the yen in efforts to curb rapidly rising trade surpluses. [R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen has been heavy, but the risk is that it hasn't gone far enough to deliver a serious scare to the markets and prevent renewed weakness in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  -- The Federal Reserve's unprecedented use of an electronic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  broking system Thursday demonstrated that even central banks - like their commercial counterparts - are trying to be more efficient. [G/FED] \par \par \uc2  --Japan's Prime Minister Hashimoto said his government plans to implement tax cuts exceeding Y4 trillion, including Y2.0 trillion of special income tax reductions this year and Y2.0 trillion next year. The government plans an economic stimulus package that will total over Y16 trillion, with Y10 trillion of real spending. \par \par \uc2  --Top Japanese companies trying to raise money overseas are beginning to feel the adverse effect of Moody's decision to change its outlook for Japan's sovereign debt to negative from stable, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-04-98 \par \par \uc2  1923GMT \par \par \uc2  1042 4190 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du49031hq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
