\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging market  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  - Yen gains boost Asia. \b0\par\par\uc2 794 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 9 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were again dominated by firmer Asia markets on Thursday which got a late boost from a plummeting dollar/yen in the wake of surprise Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the yen. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Europe, meantime, kept to tight ranges in thin, pre-holiday conditions with the Czech crown and Polish zloty idling and the rouble slightly firmer ahead of Friday's Duma vote on prime-minister designate Sergei Kiriyenko. \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held on to the bulk of their overnight gains on the back of the yen gains against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan  said it and the U.S. Federal Reserve on its behalf sold dollars for yen in afternoon Europe. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after a cool market reception to the economic stimulus steps announced by Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto earlier. \par \par \uc2  Although traders were impressed with size of the new stimulus measures for Japan - 10 trillion yen in fresh spending including four trillion in income tax cuts - there was some scepticism whether it would be enough to revive Japan's flagging domestic economy. \par \par \uc2  Asia markets also gleaned some optimism from the agreement between Indonesia and the International Monetary Fund over reforms to revive the country's economy. \par \par \uc2  Although details of the agreement will not be officially announced until Friday or Monday, sources said it was a comprehensive reform package and were aimed at bringing the rupiah down to 6,000 per dollar over time. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah stood at 7,900/8,100 in Europe against 8,400 bid in late Wednesday trade. The 8,000 area has provided a key resistance point for rupiah gains since mid-February. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the rouble firmed slightly against the dollar with the market unruffled at the likely prospect of prime-minister designate Kiriyenko being rejected at a first nomination hearing Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Russia's risk premium is up a bit on the political situation, but it's a careful market at the moment rather than one looking for the exit," said a U.S. bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said it was to be expected that Kiriyenko would not make the first cut in front of a Duma largely hostile to President Boris Yeltsin's young, reform-minded candidate. But analysts were also mindful that Yeltsin can make up to three nominations to the Duma in which time plenty of political horse-trading may ensure his candidate's eventual confirmation. \par \par \uc2  The rouble stood at 6.1255/65 per dollar, just up from its 6.1270 per dollar late Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid/offer rate was set on Thursday at 6.1070/1350 from 6.1040/1340 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty was firmer in light trade, ending Thursday trade at 6.98/6.95 percent above its parity rate against a target basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against 6.84/6.82 percent Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown, meantime was slightly weaker against the mark but above session lows. In afternoon Europe, it stood at 18.804/24 per mark from 18.709 bid Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKETS SNAPSHOT \par \par \uc2  The following is a snapshot of emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ASIA\tab \par * Indonesian rupiah\tab   7,900 per dollar bid vs 8,400 late in London on Wednesday.\par * Malaysian ringgit\tab   3,6650 per dollar bid vs 3.7100 on Wednesday. Thai baht\tab     40.00 per dollar vs 40.05 late Wednesday. Philippine peso\tab   37.50 per dollar vs 37.75.\par * Singapore dollar\tab   1.5950 per dollar versus 1.6010 late Wednesday. Indian rupee\tab   39.50 per dollar vs 39.50 Wednesday.\par EUROPE\tab \tab \par * Russian rouble\tab   at 6.1255 per dollar bid versus 6.1270 Wednesday. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  daily bid/off rates at 6.0070/6.05990 from 6.0050/6.0570 Wednesday.\par * Mark/Czech crown at 18.799 bid compared with 18.709 Wednesday. Mark/zloty at 1.8850 compared with 1.8820. Hungarian forint at 116.36 per mark from 116.20 Wednesday and Slovak crown\tab      at 19.274 against 19.246 per mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Zloty at 6.98/95 percent above its target basket parity versus 6.84/82 Wednesday. Hungarian forint 2.19 percent above basket parity vs 2.25 pct Wednesday. Slovak crown 2.10 percent below basket parity versus 2.20 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Ukrainian hryvnia\tab   at 2.0404 per dollar bid versus 2.0408 late Wednesday. Romanian leu\tab   8,420 per dollar vs 8,400.\par AFRICA\tab \tab \par * South African rand\tab   at 5.0385 per dollar vs 5.0420. Kenyan shilling\tab   60.45 vs 59.80.\par LATIN AMERICA\tab \par * Mexican peso\tab   weaker at 8.4300 per dollar vs 8.4330. Brazil's real\tab   at 1.1240 per dollar bid vs 1.1240. ((Andrew Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .news@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4907r0v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
