\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED-BOE declines comment on BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      In LONDON story 'BOE declines comment on BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' please read in third paragraph ....and that it was \par \par \uc2   assisted.... instead of ....but that it was not assisted \par \par \uc2  (correcting to make clear the BOJ said Fed had assisted the BOJ). \par \par \uc2  A corrected story follows. \par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 9 (Reuters) - The Bank of England on Thursday declined to comment on the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's  disclosure that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy yen. \par \par \uc2  In response to queries from Reuters, a BOE official said the British \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no comment to make on the developments. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Thursday, a Bank of Japan (BOJ) official said the BOJ had sold dollars for yen in the New York market and that it was assisted by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga said on Thursday that Tokyo took "decisive action" in order to stem the yen's weakness against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) spokesman told Reuters that the MOF bought yen and sold dollars at 1320 GMT at around 133.50-133.00 yen to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Federal Reserve Bank of New York said it had no comment on talk in the market that it had been selling dollars for yen on behalf of the Bank of Japan (BoJ). \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 130.25/30 yen at 1417 GMT, having earlier fallen as low as 129.52. It has slumped around five yen since late last week. \par \par \uc2  ((Adam Cox, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6784 Fax +44 171 542 5285 adam.cox@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4907mlh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
