\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday -2: Not Much Fear Of BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Today \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 1998\par 04:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Tanami and Kuroda both signaled Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to conduct dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. They reiterated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take 'proper steps' on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But dealers said there isn't much fear of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the Wednesday session, partly bacause of the perception that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't want to cause the dollar to fall too sharply before the release of its quarterly tankan survey of business sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Since the tankan is expected to show a dismal corporate outlook on the economy, which would be yen-negative, a dollar drop now would allow dealers to buy the dollar back at a bargain price after the tankan, traders reasoned. \par \par \uc2  Economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires forecast on average that the key big manufacturers' diffusion index (DI) would fall to minus 24 from minus 11 three months ago. The DI measures the percentage of companies seeing conditions improving minus those seeing conditions worsening. \par \par \uc2  In addition, many Japanese players are waiting to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dips since they've missed out on chances to buy the dollar at its recent lows, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The trust bank dealer said the dollar could drop below Y133.00 later in the day. But dollar buying demand by Japanese institutional investors is expected to lend firm support around Y132.50, other dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The mark is at Y72.06, down from Y72.28 earlier in Tokyo and a fraction lower than Y72.07 in New York late Tuesday. The mark was quoted in Tokyo late Tuesday at Y71.47. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sterling is at $1.6725, down from $1.6728 earlier in Tokyo and above\par $1.6713 in New York late Tuesday. Sterling was at $1.6785 in Tokyo late\par Tuesday.\par By Kenneth McCallum; 813-5255-2942; kmccallum@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-04-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0227GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4102re6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
