\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar firm across the board in morning Europe. \b0\par\par\uc2 627 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Mar 31 (Reuters) - The dollar made a strong start across the board in Europe, pushing to a 2-1/2 month peak against the yen as Japan's fiscal year came to a close and testing seven month highs against the mark and Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the ongoing pessimism over Japan's economy and the anticipation of capital outflows from Japan once the new fiscal year starts on Wednesday saw the yen marked lower against the dollar and mark. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off Japanese officials' protestation of excessive yen weakness and as the fiscal year closed, showed less concern over Bank of Japan support for the yen. \par \par \uc2  A rise in Japan's benchmark Nikkei stock index still left it well short of its close of 18,003 at the end of fiscal 1996/97, implying unrealised losses on banks' equity holdings, said analysts. \par \par \uc2  This gave the dollar, already firm from growing anticipation of huge capital outflows from Japan as the new fiscal year starts, a late boost in Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  "Historically, those who have argued for these seasonal patterns have been disappointed, but this is an unusual fiscal year-end," said Francis Breedon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  Deregulation of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market gets under way on April 1 which is seen easing investors' capital flows out of Japan, providing a drag on the yen. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, the ongoing gloom over Japan's economy is likely to be exacerbated by Thursday's Bank of Japan quarterly corporate sentiment survey. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was trading at 133.29/39 at 0810 GMT, down from an earlier peak of 133.48, its highest point since January 7. It stood at 131.92/2.01 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Mark/yen was at 72.00/05, just off a fresh 2-1/2 month high of 72.10 yen but well above 71.60/65 yen Monday. \par \par \uc2  Wariness over Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop the yen still lingers but dealers say there has been little sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese authorities have been dropping huge hints threatening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but until they back it up with action the yen is a one-way bet at the moment," said Lee Ferridge, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar in Europe, meantime, was also scoring fresh highs against the mark and Swiss franc. The dollar/yen gains were providing general dollar support, but sterling/mark's push to an 8-1/2 year high was helping support dollar/mark. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of dollar/mark support is coming from sterling/mark while the search for yield is hitting the low-yielding Swiss franc and yen. All these factors are coming together right now," said Commerzbank's Ferridge. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark was trading at 1.8483/93, down from its earlier seven-month peak of 1.8540 marks but up from 1.8416/21 late Monday. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar stood at 1.5225/35, down from its 7-1/2 month peak of 1.5275 francs and up from Monday's 1.5152/62. \par \par \uc2  The focus today is on today's monetary policy-setting Federal Open Market Committee meeting in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Few expect U.S. interest rates to be changed at this meeting, but dealers said the market's preference is to be long dollars going into today's meeting. \par \par \uc2  On the data front, eyes are on U.S. March consumer confidence data at 1500 GMT and the Chicago purchasing managers' index for March, forecast to show a slight dip to 57.3 from 57.8 previously. ((Andrew Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011004du3v00j5l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
