\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar powers to 11-week high vs yen in late Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0610 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     132.47/57\tab \tab 132.60-131.40\par  USD/DEM     1.8471/81\tab \tab 1.8485-1.8455\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 31 (Reuters) - The dollar rose to its highest \par \par \uc2  level against the yen since mid-January by late Tokyo trade on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, buoyed by expectations its uptrend would continue when \par \par \uc2  Japan's new fiscal year starts on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dollar buying picked up in late afternoon trade after \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's 225-share Nikkei stock index managed to post only a \par \par \uc2  modest 1.62 percent gain on the last day of fiscal 1997/98. \par \par \uc2  "People were hesitant to buy dollars too aggressively due to speculation that public funds might substantially boost the Nikkei," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But such speculation faded as the Nikkei continued to hover substantially below 18,000 by late afternoon," he added. \par \par \uc2  The key 225-share Nikkei average ended Tuesday's session up 264.13 points at 16,527.17. \par \par \uc2  Senior members of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) had said they hoped to push the Nikkei to last fiscal year's closing level of 18,003 by March 31, to prevent banks and corporations from suffering big losses on stockholdings. \par \par \uc2  Dollar buying in the afternoon was mostly led by overseas operators, as most Japanese interbank players remained on the sidelines due to fiscal year-end book-closing. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar buying related to the setting up of new investment trust funds also helped to boost the greenback. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar slipped to as low as 131.40 yen on comments by Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara, who said Japan would do anything if necessary to cope with excessive weakness of the yen. \par \par \uc2  "We will do everything if necessary," he said when asked about the yen's weakening to over 132 yen against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar quickly pared its losses by mid-morning due to substantial commercial dollar buying by Japanese operators. \par \par \uc2  The greenback had been well supported from early trade on by speculation more than $1 billion worth of commercial dollar buying from Japanese banks could emerge at 0100 GMT Tokyo fixing, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar briefly slipped in late morning on a report from Jiji news service that the head of the Japanese government's Tax Commission, Hiroshi Kato, had proposed income and corporate tax cuts worth about 10 trillion yen, to be funded by sales of government assets. \par \par \uc2  But the Jiji report failed to cool off dollar bulls - as did comments by Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the International Finance Bureau of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , who said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants should "deal earnestly" with current dollar/yen movements. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda also told reporters later that an excessive weakness in the yen was undesirable. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese institutional investors are very keen to invest in foreign securities in the new fiscal year, so they are likely to stampede to buy dollars at every bargain-hunting opportunity," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The market was still cautious about possible dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to reverse the yen's downtrend, although it could temporarily help to slow the dollar's rise, they said. \par \par \uc2  "People are cautious that the BOJ might step in soon to halt the yen's fall, but the dollar is still likely to test this year's high within the next few days," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit a 1998 high of 134.45 on January 7 in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  In late Tuesday trade in Tokyo, the dollar briefly climbed as high as 132.80 yen. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 131.93/03 yen and 1.8479/84 marks in New York on Monday. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3v08ggv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
