\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Tokyo Yen Volatilities Up On Lower Spot \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 07:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Volatilities implied by Japanese yen and Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options are higher in Tokyo Monday compared with their levels in New York late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Buying demand from Japanese investors ahead of the fiscal year-end on March 31 pushed the dollar up versus the yen in the spot market, helping to lift dollar-yen volatilities, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'Japanese buying pushed the (dollar-yen) spot up and therefore the volatilities,' said a trader at a Japanese bank. Fears of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also added to the higher dollar-yen options. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to see initial resistance around Y130.80 ahead of stiffer resistance around Y131.30, as the possibility of yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighs on the dollar, traders said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns were underscored by comments from the top two bureaucrats at Japan's finance ministry, saying that a weak yen is undesirable. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Monday, Eisuke Sakakibara, the vice finance minister for international affairs, said 'Excessive yen weakness is problematic.' His comments were later reiterated by Koji Tanami, the ministry's administrative vice minister. \par \par \uc2  In the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options imply volatility of 13.3% bid, up from 13.0% in New York Friday, but below 13.5% in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the mark, they are higher at 8.1% from 7.9% in New York Friday. Dollar/mark options were quoted at 7.5% in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0510 GMT (12:10 a.m. EST), the dollar is at Y130.65, up from Y130.35 late Friday in New York, and DM1.8273, slightly down from DM1.8275 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Risk-reversals favor dollar put options against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either put or call options by the premium or discount applied. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0518GMT \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3u02p4h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
