\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar marches above 131 yen as Tokyo stocks slide. \b0\par\par\uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0615 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     131.15/20\tab \tab 131.00-129.95\par  USD/DEM     1.8280/85\tab \tab 1.8285-1.8260\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 30 (Reuters) - The dollar marched above 131 \par \par \uc2  yen in late Monday afternoon, buoyed by substantial buying from \par \par \uc2  overseas operators as well as domestic investors. \par \par \uc2      Yen sales accelerated in late afternoon as the Tokyo stock \par \par \uc2  market dived despite widespread hopes the Japanese government \par \par \uc2  would boost stocks ahead of March 31, when many corporations in \par \par \uc2  Tokyo close their books, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Market participants had expected the government's price-keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to effectively boost the key Nikkei-225 stock average above 18,000 on Tuesday so banks could earn net unrealised profits on their equity holdings. \par \par \uc2  But the Nikkei finished on Monday at 16,263.04, down 2.84 percent or 476.22 points from its previous close, and far lower than 18,003, the level the index finished at on the previous 1996/97 business year. \par \par \uc2  "We have been concerned how much above 18,000 the Nikkei would end on Tuesday, but now we are worried if the Nikkei can manage to stay above 16,000," said a European bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  If the Nikkei index finishes on Tuesday far lower than the previous business year end, that would revive concerns over Japan's financial system, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Those who had been hesitant in dollar buying were rushing into the market this afternoon. They were mainly (Japanese) institutional investors," said a trust bank dealer. It may be possible to say that the dollar will never fall decisively below 130 yen for the rest of this century, he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Japanese economic data was expected to remain bearish for the yen for now. February industrial production levels, released on Monday, fell further than expected. \par \par \uc2  Japan industrial output fell 3.3 percent in February from January and was expected to fall 2.5 percent month-on-month in both March and April, the Trade Ministry said. \par \par \uc2  But aggressive buying was curbed by concerns over possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). The BOJ last stepped in just above 131 yen earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  A senior U.S. bank dealer said, however, those who sold dollars due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears had to cover their shorts later, and such short-covering helped the late rally. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, there was expectation of large commercial dollar buying on Tuesday, providing another support for the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  The buying may partly stem from Japanese banks which close their books on Tuesday, related to writing-off of their bad loans to Asia and other regions. \par \par \uc2  Japanese banks usually raise dollar-denominated funds for such lending and a decision to write off loans would require them to repay their procured funds in dollars, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Given bearish prospects for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , remarks from senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) officials on Monday had little impact on dollar/yen trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market was, however, cautious about more talk of possible income tax cuts by Japanese politicians, they said. \par \par \uc2  Senior MOF official Haruhiko Kuroda said that current \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels were excessive, and that MOF maintained the position that it would act decisively against excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. In an earlier media report, senior MOF official Eisuke Sakakibara said an excessive yen fall was problematic. \par \par \uc2  On Sunday, Taku Yamasaki, ruling Liberal Democratic Party policy chief, said that the government will decide on large-scale tax cuts at around the time leaders of the Group of Seven industrialised nations meet in mid-May. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 130.35/45 yen and 1.8260/70 marks in New York on Friday. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3 3432-8570 fax +81-3 3432-7462, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3u08dvk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
