\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar looks for inspiration from Japan and Buba. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,066 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 27 (Reuters) - The dollar steadied more than one percent above its overnight lows against the yen as traders awaited more details of Japan's economic stimulus plans. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, dollar/mark settled into tight ranges before the release of a Bundesbank report on economic convergence in the European Union ahead of economic and monetary union. \par \par \uc2  "The yen and the EMU report are the two key things today, but given that it is anyone's guess how the mark will react to the Bundesbank's report, any surprise is more likely to come from that front," said Julian Jessop, economist at Nikko Europe International in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 129.10/20 yen at 0857 GMT, stronger than its overnight low of 127.78 and 128.67/72 late in Europe on Thursday. It was at 1.8206/11 marks from 1.8214/24 yesterday. \par \par \uc2  The yen has drawn little sustained support after measures worth 16 trillion yen were proposed on Thursday by Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party, even though the package was larger than traders had been expecting. \par \par \uc2  That is because of uncertainty about whether income tax cuts will be part of the stimulus measures and a rift between LDP officials about whether to delay fiscal reforms which require Japan to stop issuing deficit financing bonds by 2003/04. \par \par \uc2  There is also concern that the measures will not be enough to revive Japan's stalled economy. \par \par \uc2  "The package in Japan has received a bad press and though it was larger than expected, in the absence of income tax cuts, it may not be enough to turn the economy around," said Gerard Lyons, chief economist at DKB International in London. \par \par \uc2  Lyons said he expects wariness of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep dollar/yen capped until early next week but predicted that Japan's quarterly tankan survey of business sentiment out on Wednesday would be weak enough to trigger renewed yen slippage. \par \par \uc2  Within Europe, the focus was on the report on EMU which the Bundesbank is to publish later on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders are not expecting the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's report to unsettle expectations that 11 European Union countries will found EMU as recommended on Wednesday by the European Commission. \par \par \uc2  Bavarian premier Edmund Stoiber said on Friday the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believed EMU could go ahead as planned in 1999. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, any criticisms the Bundesbank makes of economic convergence efforts are expected to have already been made by the European Monetary Institute, which called on Wednesday for EU nations to continue to consolidate their fiscal positions. \par \par \uc2  Traders are therefore expecting limited \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaction to the report. To be sure, the lira could be vulnerable to setbacks if Italy is singled out for criticism, they said. \par \par \uc2  Italy's Il Sole-24 Ore newspaper said the Bundesbank will ask Italy for "guarantees" of a credible debt reduction plan and severe fiscal discipline. The paper cited German government sources as saying they did not rule out the possibility the document could be critical of Italy's financial situation. \par \par \uc2  Traders will be looking for clues to the Bundesbank's thinking from the speech council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher is to deliver from 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Later on Friday, U.S. personal income and spending statistics for February will be released at 1330 GMT. Also, Robert McTeer, president of the Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas, speaks at 1445 GMT. ((Swaha Pattanaik, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6284, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 129.10/20 yen at 0857 GMT, stronger than its overnight low of 127.78 and 128.67/72 late in Europe on Thursday. It was at 1.8206/11 marks from 1.8214/24 yesterday. \par \par \uc2  The yen has drawn little sustained support after measures worth 16 trillion yen were proposed on Thursday by Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party, even though the package was larger than traders had been expecting. \par \par \uc2  That is because of uncertainty about whether income tax cuts will be part of the stimulus measures and a rift between LDP officials about whether to delay fiscal reforms which require Japan to stop issuing deficit financing bonds by 2003/04. \par \par \uc2  There is also concern that the measures will not be enough to revive Japan's stalled economy. \par \par \uc2  "The package in Japan has received a bad press and though it was larger than expected, in the absence of income tax cuts, it may not be enough to turn the economy around," said Gerard Lyons, chief economist at DKB International in London. \par \par \uc2  Lyons said he expects wariness of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep dollar/yen capped until early next week but predicted that Japan's quarterly tankan survey of business sentiment out on Wednesday would be weak enough to trigger renewed yen slippage. \par \par \uc2  Within Europe, the focus was on the report on EMU which the Bundesbank is to publish later on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders are not expecting the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's report to unsettle expectations that 11 European Union countries will found EMU as recommended on Thursday by the European Commission. \par \par \uc2  Bavarian premier Edmund Stoiber said on Friday the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believed EMU could go ahead as planned in 1999. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, any criticisms the Bundesbank makes of economic convergence efforts are expected to have already been made by the European Monetary Institute, which called on Wednesday for EU nations to continue to consolidate their fiscal positions. \par \par \uc2  Traders are therefore expecting limited \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaction to the report. To be sure, the lira could be vulnerable to setbacks if Italy is singled out for criticism, they said. \par \par \uc2  Italy's Il Sole-24 Ore newspaper said the Bundesbank will ask Italy for "guarantees" of a credible debt reduction plan and severe fiscal discipline. The paper cited German government sources as saying they did not rule out the possibility the document could be critical of Italy's financial situation. \par \par \uc2  Traders will be looking for clues to the Bundesbank's thinking from the speech council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher is to deliver from 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Later on Friday, U.S. personal income and spending statistics for February will be released at 1330 GMT. Also, Robert McTeer, president of the Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas, speaks at 1445 GMT. ((Swaha Pattanaik, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6284, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3r08iuz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
