\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar powers up vs yen by late Tokyo trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0629 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     129.18/28\tab \tab 129.28-127.78\par  USD/DEM     1.8215/25\tab \tab 1.8223-1.8195\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 27 (Reuters) - The dollar strengthened against \par \par \uc2  the yen by late trade in Tokyo on Friday, rising about 1-1/2 \par \par \uc2  yen from its early lows on active short-covering and aggressive \par \par \uc2  bids led by Japanese investors and importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Late falls in the benchmark Nikkei stock index and prices \par \par \uc2  of Japanese government bond (JGB) futures had depressed the \par \par \uc2  yen's undertone by late trade, they said. \par \par \uc2  A bearish mood in overseas markets had carried over into early trade in Tokyo, with the dollar dipping as low as 127.78 yen on speculative selling aimed at triggering stop-loss sell orders around 128 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the fall was short-lived as a wave of bids quickly boosted the dollar from its low. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they detected purchases from Japanese life and non-life insurers, trust banks and importers. Asian central banks were rumoured to have bought aggressively. \par \par \uc2  Short-holders were forced to unwind their positions, and this accelerated the dollar's uptrend, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Activity slowed in the afternoon, with short-covering continuing but operators reluctant to build new positions due to caution over possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official Haruhiko Kuroda commented on Friday that a weak yen was not favourable. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda, director-general of MOF's International Finance Bureau, also told reporters the overnight strengthening of the yen against the dollar was a move "in the right direction". \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 128.43/48 yen and 1.8198/08 marks in late New York trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said uncertainty over possible future income tax cuts also helped to cap the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Taku Yamasaki, policy chief of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP), said on Thursday Japan might decide to cut income taxes while fleshing out an economic stimulus package, the outline of which was unveiled on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Expectations that Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto would decide on income tax cuts before the mid-May Group of Seven (G7) nations' summit in Birmingham, England could become a supportive factor for the yen in coming weeks, said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "There is speculation among some overseas operators that Japan may still decide to cut income taxes in the future. Since the LDP unveiled its package yesterday, the market has lacked incentives," a senior Japanese city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But even without strong factors, various Japanese operators seem to have substantial dollar buying needs ahead of fiscal book closing (on March 31)," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Several dealers said there could be dollar-buying demand from some Japanese banks before their book closings and that such buying, aimed at writing off overseas losses, could be a supporting factor for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported on Wednesday that Fuji Bank would boost its reserves before the end of March in preparation for possible losses from loans to other economically-troubled Asian nations. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was speculation that other banks might do the same thing before the end of March. ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3r08ijn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
