\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr up in Tokyo,but cuts gains after Kuroda remark. \b0\par\par\uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0312 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     128.92/02\tab \tab    129.17-127.78\par  USD/DEM     1.8210/15\tab \tab    1.8223-1.8195\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 27 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher against \par \par \uc2  the yen by midday in Tokyo on Friday, lifted by strong \par \par \uc2  bargain-hunting from Japanese institutional investors and \par \par \uc2  importers. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback pared gains after a comment by senior \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official Haruhiko Kuroda that a weak \par \par \uc2  yen is not favourable. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda, director-general of MOF's International Finance Bureau, also told reporters that the overnight strengthening of the yen against the dollar was a move "in the right direction". \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a trust bank said: "A lot of Japanese investors are eager to buy dollars. But the market is cautious about buying the dollar above 129 yen in the near term due to worries about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar dropped to as low as 127.78 yen on speculative selling aimed at triggering stop-loss sell orders around 128 yen. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar quickly moved back above 128 yen on strong bargain-hunting by Japanese institutional investors and importers. \par \par \uc2  "Due to higher interest rates abroad, more money is expected to flow out of Japan after the new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  law takes effect," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "So a lot of investors are very eager to use every opportunity to bargain-hunt the dollar." \par \par \uc2  The new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, which takes effect on April 1, will liberalise all cross-border capital transactions except in the case of economic sanctions and some direct investments. \par \par \uc2  Buying related to the setting up of fresh investment trust funds also contributed to the dollar's rebound, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose above 129 yen in late morning after earlier sellers were forced to buy back the dollar to cut losses. \par \par \uc2  In addition to speculation of possible dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , uncertainties about future income tax cuts also helped to cap the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Taku Yamasaki, policy chief of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party, said Thursday Japan may decide to cut income taxes in the process of fleshing out its economic stimulus package, the outline of which was unveiled on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Expectations that Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto might decide on income tax cuts before the mid-May Group of Seven (G7) nations' summit in Birmingham, England, could become a yen-supportive factor in coming weeks, said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "To support the yen and Tokyo stocks, the government may want to keep such expectations alive as long as possible," he said. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the demand-supply condition was in favour of the dollar before the end of the fiscal year on March 31. \par \par \uc2  More setting-up of trust funds that invest in foreign securities is expected early next week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Apart from worries about BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there isn't any reason to refrain from buying dollars," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "If the dollar is heading towards 140 yen in the medium term, why not buy dollars at current levels?" \par \par \uc2  The dollar was little changed against the mark after trading in a very tight range. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 128.43/48 yen and 1.8198/08 marks in New York on Thursday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3r08ig1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
