\par\par \b \uc2  Yen Cross - Most units softer before LDP package. \b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 26 (Reuters) - Major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were under slight downward pressure against the yen in cross trade on Thursday due to jitters over the ruling Liberal Democratic Party's (LDP) announcement of the outline of an economic package later in the day, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Major units fell against the yen overseas on Wednesday due to stop-loss sales and talk of yen buying from some European central banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The mark's top remained heavy in trade here and was completely capped due to persistent selling interest ahead of the package," said a cross-yen trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, there was talk of mark buying against the yen overnight from major U.S. hedge funds, which gave the mark support, he said. \par \par \uc2  "But if buyers such as U.S. funds stop bidding, there is a risk that the mark will fall to around 70 yen or even lower," he added. \par \par \uc2  Stop-loss mark sales orders are seen in place at around 70.30 yen, with a clear break of that point seen sending it to an important support level of 70 yen, he added. \par \par \uc2  The mark was quoted at 70.54/57 yen at 0310 GMT, down from 70.60 yen in late New York trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The economic stimulus package, which the LDP is to vet in a series of meetings during the day and announce at around 5 p.m. (0800 GMT), will be worth at least 12 trillion yen ($93.0 billion), the business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun and public broadcaster NHK reported. \par \par \uc2  "Interbank traders who had built up heavy yen short positions last week were unwinding the positions this week," said a trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The yen was bought overnight in New York, prompted by a report from consultancy Medley Global Advisors, which suggested the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the dollar down towards 125 yen. Medley Global declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  The European bank dealer said, however: "I think that the yen's recent falls were within the realm of an adjustment." \par \par \uc2  "The LDP's stimulus package would not lead to further yen buying, even if politicians hint on the possibility of future tax cuts by revising the fiscal reform law," he added. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at 215.87/216.00 yen at 0311 GMT against 216.06 yen in late New York trade on Wednesday, while the Swiss franc was at 86.31/36 yen against 86.38 yen. \par \par \uc2  There was talk that a European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought yen for Swiss franc overnight, probably in relation with commercial needs or reserve adjustments, dealers said. ((Tokyo treasury Desk 81-3-3432-1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3q08og7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
