\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Japan package fails to shake yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Mar 26 (Reuters) - The yen took centre stage in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Thursday amid the unveiling of a much-anticipated Japanese economic stimulus package, but tight yen ranges persisted as the measures fell short of expectations. \par \par \uc2  Although the size of the package was impressive - well above expectations at 16 trillion yen - the emphasis of the measures were on public works spending and the lack of clear proposals on income tax cuts left dealers in London frustrated. \par \par \uc2  "The market is getting used to the build-up and then the deflation that surrounds these packages so yen ranges have been tight and volume pretty thin," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen dipped as low as 128.38 overnight in a knee-jerk reaction to the package's size. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar soon recovered to a narrow one-yen range around 129 in Europe as the ruling Liberal Democratic Party's draft measures offered few details on fiscal spending and even less on the likelihood of income tax cuts to stimulate Japan's moribund economy. \par \par \uc2  "It is not clear whether there will be any tax cuts or not and the way it is being announced is really a disaster given how much money they are going to spend," said Juergen Lindemann, senior trader at IBJ International in London. \par \par \uc2  Exceptions were high that today's package would include the income tax cuts called for by domestic businesses and U.S. policymakers to spur domestic demand in Japan. \par \par \uc2  LDP officials said details of the package will be made in April, keeping speculation of such cuts alive. But with the seasonal fiscal year-end repatriation ending next week and a likely gloomy Bank of Japan quarterly Tankan survey also next week, the yen will likely remain under pressure. \par \par \uc2  "The repatriation of funds coming to an end, the change in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulation and a weak Tankan could all fuel yen selling," said Klaus Kusber, analyst at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson. \par \par \uc2  Kusber sees potential dollar/yen upside to 135 in the near-term but is mindful that a market already short yen will not be adding to those positions with the gusto it had last year and early this year. \par \par \uc2  Nervousness over Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen weakness is providing one of the only near-term yen supports, a situation that is likely to hold sway in the market until the fiscal year ends on March 31. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat has been a factor in blocking dollar/yen, but it's hard to see the BOJ acting this side of 132 yen given the weak Japan outlook," said the U.S. bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen stood at 128.69/79 in late Europe, just down from 128.98/9.03 yen late Wednesday. Mark/yen was trading at 70.65/68 from 70.57/60. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark crept lower in late trade but was holding above 1.82 and keeping within its recent ranges. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect little impact from Friday's Bundesbank report on economic convergence towards Europe's economic and monetary union. Although criticism is likely for high debt countries Italy and Belgium, the Bundesbank's report is not seen straying far from the Dutch \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's and European Monetary Institute's EMU progress reports delivered Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling proved to be the star of an otherwise lacklustre session, making a late push to fresh eight-month highs against the mark and near four-month highs on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  It found support from Bank of England Monetary Policy Committee member Willem Buiter's comments that sterling's rise may unwind as EMU launch doubts fade, creating inflation risk. But he also implied that Asia turbulence and the recent UK budget may have eased pressure to raise rates. \par \par \uc2  Sterling/mark at 3.0720/30, down from a peak of 3.0755, while cable stood at $1.6866/76, just off $1.6876. ((A.Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3q08l6g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
