\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar ends higher in U.S., tame German CPI props. \b0\par\par\uc2 603 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 24 (Reuters) - Dollar/mark ended firmer on signs that German inflation remains contained but trading was generally listless ahead of key reports on European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) due Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also drifted up versus the yen, but kept to a narrow range as traders sat on their hands anticipating a package of measures to stoke the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  "What they're probably waiting for is to see what kind of fiscal stimulus comes out of Japan and until then I guess the dollar is going to be very quiet," said Mark Remigio, a vice president at Bank of Tokyo-Mitubishi in New York. \par \par \uc2  Several of the largest German states reported consumer prices were tame in March, while Bonn released preliminary data showing prices in West Germany fell 0.2 percent in March and rose just 1.0 percent in the past 12 months. \par \par \uc2  Some investors switched into dollars from marks, betting that Germany would not need to raise interest rates in order to slow its economy and keep price rises in check. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to 1.8277/82 marks from 1.8268/73 marks at the open and to 130.25/30 yen from 130.05/15 yen. \par \par \uc2  Mark sales were tempered in advance of separate reports due from the European Commission and the European Monetary Institute - forerunner of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - on how economic convergence is proceeding among nations hoping to join in the launch of the euro, on January 1. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think they'll point fingers at any particular country for failed fiscal policy or shortcomings on convergence criteria," said David Gilmore, a partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics. \par \par \uc2  "If people are worried about Italy being singled out it's just not going to happen. If anything it probably represents more calming of concern about the euro launch and more strength for the deutschemark," he added. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, Japan is due to present a plan to boost its flagging economy. The yen had been a bit on the defensive after Tokyo this week seemed to rule out an income tax cut, considered by many economists the key to reviving growth. \par \par \uc2  But yen bears kept to the sidelines Tuesday after Haruhiko Kuroda, director general of the finance ministry's international finance bureau, overnight said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a little too weak and threatened to take appropriate action. \par \par \uc2  Also unnerving the markets, influential finance official Eisuke Sakakibara said on Tuesday that Japan is discussing the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with the United States. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen stayed in a tight orbit around 130.20 for most of the New York session, with traders still nervous after unconfirmed reports of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  above 131 late last week. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark tapped 1.8303 in early U.S. before the small rally fizzled. The overnight low just under 1.8250 was left alone, with dealers citing key chart support near that level. \par \par \uc2  The dollar reacted little to another banner day on Wall Street, dealers said. The Dow Jones industrial stock average jumped 88 points to 8904, two points shy of a record, while the Nasdaq and S&P 500 indexes closed at new all-time highs. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the pound was flat at $1.6745/55. The dollar rose to 1.4901/06 Swiss francs from 1.4895/05 at the open and fell to Canadian $1.4155/60 from C$1.4205/10. The Australian dollar fell to $0.6705/10 from $0.6716/21. \par \par \uc2  ((-Alden Bentley, 212 859 1667)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3o08tix\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
