\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE- \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  market readies for EMU reports. \b0\par\par\uc2 506 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets held steady on Tuesday convinced that European policymakers on Wednesday will recommend 11 states as founding members of Europe's economic and monetary union (EMU). \par \par \uc2  The mark was steady on its European crosses in afternoon trade ahead of Wednesday's reports from the European Commission and the European Monetary Institute on the progress of economic convergence among EMU first wave hopefuls. \par \par \uc2  "The focus of tomorrow's attention will be mainly on Italy," said Audrey Childe-Freeman, European economist at CIBC Wood Gundy in London. \par \par \uc2  "As far as the EMI report is concerned they will endorse a more cautious view on the sustainability of the Italian fiscal policy and more specifically on the sustainability of the Italian public debt," CIBC's Childe-Freeman said. \par \par \uc2  Italy's debt-to-GDP ratio is more than twice that of the 60 percent target in the Maastricht Treaty. However, Italian newspapers said a provisional draft of the EC's report stated that Italy has reached a high level of convergence and should meet the 60 percent target by 2016. \par \par \uc2  Mark/lira remained nearly unchanged from Monday's close trading at 984.94/5.05 in afternoon Europe. \par \par \uc2  The mark held relatively steady against the other European crosses on Tuesday as the market also took stock of reports of benign German inflation. \par \par \uc2  Tame consumer price reports from four West German states released on Tuesday further dampened the possibility of a rise in German interest rates soon, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The EC is expected to release at 1000 GMT on Wednesday its recommendations on which countries qualified to launch EMU in January 1999. At the same time, the Commission releases its EU-wide economic forecasts and the EMI, the forerunner of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , releases its own report on convergence. \par \par \uc2  European Union sources and economists said on Tuesday that it would be a surprise if the European Commission (EC) did not recommend an 11 country EMU start. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said a few well-placed warnings in the reports and speeches may be enough to keep EMU members in line once they have been recommended by the EC. \par \par \uc2  "It seems to be the case that there are going to be a few tough words on convergence and that will be one way to ensure that Italy will continue on the path of structuring its economy towards EMU convergence," said Jesper Dannesboe, treasury economist at ABN AMRO in London. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the dollar stood at 130.19/24, keeping to the middle of a near-one yen session range. It stood at 130.27/32 late Monday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said pessimism over Japan's economy is keeping the bias towards yen weakness, but concerns of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and wariness ahead of Friday's economic stimulus package are likely to see a rangebound dollar/yen for now. \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Casciato, London newsroom +44 171 542 8968, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3o08t9r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
