\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/yen seen hobbled for now by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fear. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,034 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 24 (Reuters) - The dollar was raring to resume its climb against the yen at midsession Europe amid pessimism about Japan's economic outlook, but was hobbled for the time being by wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Comments made on Tuesday by several senior Japanese Finance Ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials fanned speculation that the Bank of Japan will act to curb further yen weakness by selling dollars, possibly with the help of the U.S.. \par \par \uc2  Such concern can, however, only temporarily cap dollar/yen if a Japanese economic stimulus package due to be unveiled later this week is deemed to be inadequate, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is giving short-term support to the yen but if the fiscal package is disappointing, we will see renewed upward pressure on dollar/yen," said Nick Stamenkovic, economist at DKB in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 130.29/39 yen at 1122 GMT from 130.27/32 late in Europe on Monday and the two-month high of 131.30 it hit on Friday. The mark was at 71.27/32 from 71.32/35 yesterday. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, a senior Japanese Finance Ministry official, raised the spectre of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after he said overnight the yen was too weak and that Japan would take appropriate measures to combat its weakness. \par \par \uc2  The risk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly with the U.S. began to be mooted after Eisuke Sakakibara, vice minister for international affairs at the Finance Ministry, said on Tuesday Japan was discussing the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with the U.S.. \par \par \uc2  Also, Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said while the market should generally correct excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves on its own, a case could sometimes be made for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There is a growing possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dollar/yen this week, and there is a good chance the Fed could come in with the Bank of Japan," said Lee Ferridge, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  DKB's Stamenkovic was less convinced that the U.S. would join in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said its help would depend on how strenuously \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  worked to revive its economy. This week's stimulus package is not, however, expected to do enough to boost growth and may spark new yen losses, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also buoyant against the mark, bolstered by weaker-than-expected consumer price reports from west German states. Inflation in Bavaria was at 1.1 percent for March and at 1.0 percent in Hesse and North-Rhine Westphalia. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke said on Tuesday that he saw no danger on German inflation in light of the Hesse data. \par \par \uc2  "The good news on German inflation is slightly negative for the mark," said Stamenkovic at DKB. \par \par \uc2  The next focal point for the mark is the release of reports on which countries should launch European economic and monetary union in 1999. The European Commission and the European Monetary Institute publish recommendations on Wednesday. The Bundesbank reports on economic convergence in the European Union on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Still, "the reports are unlikely to present many problems for the market which is still fairly certain 11 countries will be in EMU" at the outset, said Chris Furness, senior market strategist at 4CAST in London. \par \par \uc2  "The possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is giving short-term support to the yen but if the fiscal package is disappointing, we will see renewed upward pressure on dollar/yen," said Nick Stamenkovic, economist at DKB in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 130.29/39 yen at 1122 GMT from 130.27/32 late in Europe on Monday and the two-month high of 131.30 it hit on Friday. The mark was at 71.27/32 from 71.32/35 yesterday. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, a senior Japanese Finance Ministry official, raised the spectre of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after he said overnight the yen was too weak and that Japan would take appropriate measures to combat its weakness. \par \par \uc2  The risk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly with the U.S. began to be mooted after Eisuke Sakakibara, vice minister for international affairs at the Finance Ministry, said on Tuesday Japan was discussing the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with the U.S.. \par \par \uc2  Also, Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said while the market should generally correct excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves on its own, a case could sometimes be made for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There is a growing possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dollar/yen this week, and there is a good chance the Fed could come in with the Bank of Japan," said Lee Ferridge, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  DKB's Stamenkovic was less convinced that the U.S. would join in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said its help would depend on how strenuously \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  worked to revive its economy. This week's stimulus package is not, however, expected to do enough to boost growth and may spark new yen losses, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also buoyant against the mark, bolstered by weaker-than-expected consumer price reports from west German states. Inflation in Bavaria was at 1.1 percent for March and at 1.0 percent in Hesse and North-Rhine Westphalia. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke said on Tuesday that he saw no danger on German inflation in light of the Hesse data. \par \par \uc2  "The good news on German inflation is slightly negative for the mark," said Stamenkovic at DKB. \par \par \uc2  The next focal point for the mark is the release of reports on which countries should launch European economic and monetary union in 1999. The European Commission and the European Monetary Institute publish recommendations on Wednesday. The Bundesbank reports on economic convergence in the European Union on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Still, "the reports are unlikely to present many problems for the market which is still fairly certain 11 countries will be in EMU" at the outset, said Chris Furness, senior market strategist at 4CAST in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 1.8292/97 marks at 1213 GMT from 1.8271/76 late in Europe on Monday. ((Swaha Pattanaik, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6284, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3o08sfa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
