\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr down on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears, LDP tax remarks. \b0\par\par\uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0312 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     129.99/09\tab \tab    130.77-129.80\par  USD/DEM     1.8258/68\tab \tab    1.8264-1.8244\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 24 (Reuters) - The dollar was down against the \par \par \uc2  yen on long liquidation by midday in Tokyo on Tuesday, amid \par \par \uc2  lingering fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The greenback also came under pressure after Koichi Kato, \par \par \uc2  secretary-general of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party \par \par \uc2  (LDP), said the party wanted to convene a panel soon to discuss \par \par \uc2  possible future tax cuts. \par \par \uc2  Kato told a news conference after a meeting of LDP executives on Tuesday that he had told party members to consider as soon as possible ways to cut income taxes. \par \par \uc2  If the party believed a permanent large tax cut would have a significant impact on consumption, which would be good for the economy, then Japan should change its fiscal reform law, Kato said. \par \par \uc2  "More players liquidated dollar longs after Kato's remarks. The dollar may slide further if stop-loss orders between 129.50 and 129.80 yen are triggered," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar rose on expectations of commercial dollar buying ahead of 0100 GMT Tokyo fixing, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar demand related to the setting up of fresh investment trust funds also helped push the dollar higher in early trade. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar headed lower in mid-morning after comments by senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) officials triggered loss-cut dollar sales by earlier buyers. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, the MOF's vice minister for international affairs, said on Tuesday that Japan is discussing the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and other issues with the United States. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara declined to comment further on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Separately, Haruhiko Kuroda, director-general of MOF's International Finance Bureau, told reporters on Tuesday the yen is a little too weak and the MOF will take appropriate action. \par \par \uc2  "As we have been saying, the yen is a little too weak and we will take appropriate action," Kuroda said, adding: "We would prefer the yen to be a little stronger." \par \par \uc2  "The market was quite jittery about the possibility of BOJ (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so people liquidated dollar longs after those comments by the two MOF officials," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar was supported by bargain-hunting interest from Japanese institutional investors and importers at around 129.50 yen and below. \par \par \uc2  The outlook for the yen remained bearish after the LDP's Kato said on Monday that an economic package the party plans to outline this week would not include income tax cuts, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Politicians are making hints of income tax cuts in the future, but that future is so distant. The politicians do not seem to be addressing the urgent needs of the economy," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  The LDP is expected to announce on Thursday the outline of an economic package worth more than 10 trillion yen, and to reveal details of the package in April. \par \par \uc2  The dollar remained stuck in an extremely tight range against the mark in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 130.42/52 yen and 1.8257/67 marks in New York on Monday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3o08r4y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
