\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar/yen battles to overcome  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 24 (Reuters) - The dollar and the mark battled to make headway against the yen, struggling to overcome renewed talk of Japanese income tax cuts and wariness of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Several senior Japanese Finance Ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials spoke about the yen on Tuesday, raising the spectre of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , possibly co-ordinated with the U.S.. \par \par \uc2  However, failure to back these threats up soon with action will cause the yen to resume its slide, particularly if traders are disappointed by the Japanese economic stimulus package due to be unveiled this week, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "There is a growing possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dollar/yen this week, and there is a good chance the Fed could come in with the Bank of Japan," said Lee Ferridge, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  "Too any Japanese officials are being too specific and given the market has seen words before and nothing to back it up, they will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to have any impact." \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was at 129.85/95 at 0805 GMT from 130.27/32 late in Europe on Monday. Mark/yen was at 71.12/15 from 71.32/35. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, a senior Japanese Finance Ministry official, said overnight the yen was too weak. \par \par \uc2  He said Japan would take appropriate measures to combat yen weakness, a threat which took on added meaning for traders after Eisuke Sakakibara, the Finance Ministry's vice minister for international affairs, said on Tuesday that Japan was discussing the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Newly appointed Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaru Hayami also spoke of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. He said that while the market should generally be left to correct excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, there was sometimes a case to be made for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Hayami also questioned whether it was appropriate for the yen to be weak given Japan's rising current account surplus. \par \par \uc2  The yen's immediate prospects now depend on this week's stimulus package. While a senior member of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party said overnight he wants the party to consider the possibility of future income tax cuts, analysts are not expecting such a measure to be announced this week. \par \par \uc2  "In the near-term, there is a big danger of disappointment on the package so I don't fell strongly about singing the yen's praises at the moment," said Marian Bell, treasury economist at Royal Bank of Scotland in London. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, dollar/mark was bolstered by a weaker-than-expected consumer price report from the German state of Hesse. \par \par \uc2  Hesse CPI fell 0.2 percent in March and was up 1.0 percent from a year earlier. Traders are now looking to see whether inflation was as subdued in other west German states due to release CPI data later on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/mark was helped a bit because the data was weaker than expected," said Commerzbank's Ferridge. To be sure, "it still doesn't mean that the Bundesbank is going to cut rates." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 1.8282/87 marks at 0917 GMT from Tuesday's low of 1.8247 and 1.8271/76 late in Europe on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The focal point for the mark is the release of reports on which countries should launch the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The European Commission and the European Monetary Institute publish their recommendations on Wednesday while the Bundesbank reports on economic convergence in the European Union on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "It's euro, euro, euro this week," said Bell at RBS. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, traders are looking for direction from speeches Bundesbank council members are to deliver on Tuesday. Ernst Welteke speaks at 0930 GMT, Hans-Juergen Krupp speaks at 1000 GMT, and Helmut Hesse speaks at 1300 GMT. ((Swaha Pattanaik, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6284, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3o08r3c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
