\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr slips after comments by senior MOF officials. \b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 24 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0055 GMT -- \par \par \uc2      *Dollar down against yen in mid-morning Tokyo on loss-cut \par \par \uc2  selling triggered after comments by senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  (MOF) officials Eisuke Sakakibara and Haruhiko Kuroda. \par \par \uc2      *Sakakibara, MOF's vice minister for international affairs, \par \par \uc2  said Japan discussing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and other issues \par \par \uc2  with United States, but declined further comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      *Separately, Kuroda, director-general of MOF's \par \par \uc2  International Finance Bureau, told reporters yen a little too \par \par \uc2  weak, adding that MOF will take appropriate action. \par \par \uc2  *"Players who bought dollars earlier moved to liquidate their positions after Sakakibara said Japan is consulting with United States," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  *"Market is bullish about dollar, but is still cautious about BOJ's dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  *There may be stop-loss dollar sell orders around 129.80 yen, but dollar is likely to find support from solid bids from Japanese investors and importers around 129.50 yen and below, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Earlier, dollar rose as high as 130.77 yen mainly on buying related to set-up of fresh investment trust funds. \par \par \uc2  *But dollar's upside was capped by sporadic sales from Japanese exporters and fears of possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers said there was also vague talk that Bank of England (BOE) might have sold dollars for yen overnight on behalf of BOJ. \par \par \uc2  *"This kinds of talk is leaving the market cautious about pushing dollar above 131 yen," said a Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  0011 GMT - *Dollar edged higher against yen in early Tokyo trade on Tuesday, supported by commercial buying ahead of local fixing at 0100 GMT, but gains limited. \par \par \uc2  *Weakness in Nikkei average also hurt undertone of yen. Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be under stronger speculative selling pressure should Nikkei extends its losses. \par \par \uc2  *But fears over possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped topside. \par \par \uc2  *Short-term technical resistance seen around 130.80 yen and clear break above that level should pave way to 131. *As of 0026 GMT, benchmark Nikkei average fell 211.79 points or 1.26 percent at 16,657.04. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3o08r13\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
