\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar up but capped by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fear in Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0600 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     130.58/60\tab \tab 130.87-130.25\par  USD/DEM     1.8296/98\tab \tab 1.8325-1.8289\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 23 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher against \par \par \uc2  the yen by late afternoon in Tokyo on Monday, but its upside \par \par \uc2  was capped by fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \par \par \uc2  the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  The market was also cautious before the release this week \par \par \uc2  of an economic stimulus package by the Japanese government, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There are a lot of dollar bulls. But people are cautious about pushing the dollar above 131 yen after the BOJ reportedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars on Friday," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped to knock the dollar down by more than two yen at one point from the day's high of 131.30 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Sources in the government and ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) said last Friday the cabinet would on March 27 approve an economic stimulus package to be worth 10 trillion yen to 15 trillion yen and that may contain income tax cuts. \par \par \uc2  "The market is generally sceptical that the package will contain steps impressive enough to lift the yen and Tokyo stocks," said the city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But people are still cautious about holding dollar longs, as they remember vividly what happened on December 17." \par \par \uc2  On that day, Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto surprised the market by announcing a one-time special income tax cut of two trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  The announcement was followed the same day by heavy BOJ dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sent the dollar down by nearly six yen at one point from the day's high. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said sporadic dollar sales were detected from Japanese exporters, but the dollar was supported mainly by buying related to set-up of fresh investment trust funds. \par \par \uc2  Such dollar demand was expected to continue for the rest of this month, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese institutional investors and U.S. fund operators remained eager to bargain-hunt dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly pared gains in the afternoon following comments by senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official Haruhiko Kuroda saying that the recent weakness of the yen had been overdone. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda, director-general of MOF's International Finance Bureau, told a meeting sponsored by Institute of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Trade Research on Monday that Japan would act against any excessive movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "Kuroda's comments were basically the same as what he has been saying lately. So the impact was short-lived," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the surge in crude oil prices might trigger more volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market later on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "If higher oil prices rock U.S. asset markets, that might have some impact on the dollar," said a Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  NYMEX May crude futures jumped above $16 a barrel in out-of-hours trading on the ACCESS system late Sunday after Saudi Arabia, Venezuela and Mexico announced an agreement to cut world oil output. Friday's closing price was $14.61. \par \par \uc2  The dollar traded within a narrow range against the mark during Tokyo trading hours on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 130.32/42 yen and 1.8310/20 marks in New York on Friday. ((Kanta Watanabe/Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3n08x53\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
