\par\par \b \uc2  Yen Cross - Mark firms, but finds cap at 71.60 yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 23 (Reuters) - The German mark firmed against the yen in cross trade on Monday amid a lack of positive factors for the yen and limited gains on the Tokyo stock market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the mark was capped at a resistance line of around 71.60-70 yen where profit-takers were eager to sell marks for yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Many dealers agreed there were no good reasons for buying the yen against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cross trade, although the announcement of the outline of Japan's economic measures this week is serving as a tentative damper on aggressive yen sales. \par \par \uc2  "There is a caution over BOJ (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and over \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic steps, but on a long-term basis it's quite difficult to find any yen-supportive factors," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The mark was quoted at 71.41 yen at 0455 GMT against 71.18 yen in late New York trade on Friday. \par \par \uc2  U.S. operators were buying marks for yen, although trading was not heavy, said a Japanese bank trader. \par \par \uc2  He said the mark may come under a slight downward pressure in the near term before eventually testing 72 yen. \par \par \uc2  There was talk last week that some overseas funds bought longer-dated mark call options with strikes of around 74 yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the limited rise in the Tokyo stock market as a result of paring its earlier gains also discouraged yen buying. \par \par \uc2  Policy-makers' comments on possible pump-priming steps over the weekend failed to convince investors the economy would recover soon. \par \par \uc2  The key 225-share Nikkei average was up 0.32 percent or 53.35 points at 16,883.82 as of 0454 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Yen sales were slowed by remarks from senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda on Monday that the recent weakness of the yen had been overdone, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Traders in Tokyo said they would focus on the Bundesbank's report about the European economic and monetary union (EMU) on Friday to see how the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would assess 11 countries' efforts to meet criteria for becoming participants in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Sterling was 217.83/98 yen as of 0538 GMT against its 217.65 yen in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Some Japanese investors in Tokyo were intent on buying sterling against the yen on dips amid lingering expectations of higher U.K. interest rates, dealers said. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3 3432-1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3n08x3o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
