\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar eases slightly after MOF Kuroda's remarks. \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 23 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0515 GMT -- \par \par \uc2      *Dollar eased slightly against yen in afternoon Tokyo, \par \par \uc2  following comments by senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda. \par \par \uc2      *Kuroda, director-general of MOF's International Finance \par \par \uc2  Bureau, told meeting sponsored by Institute of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  and Trade Research on Monday that recent yen weakness was \par \par \uc2  overdone, adding that Japan will act against excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  movements. \par \par \uc2  *Greenback was well-supported by bargain-hunting interest from Japanese institutional investors and U.S. fund operators, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *But market was cautious about buying dollars aggressively due to fears of possible dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) and release of economic stimulus package by Japanese government this week. \par \par \uc2  *"Dollar is well-bid, but most market participants are hesitant about pushing it up above 131 yen in near term after Friday's BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers said market was cautious about how U.S. financial markets will react on Monday to surge in crude oil prices. \par \par \uc2  *NYMEX May crude futures jumped above $16 a barrel in out-of-hours trading on ACCESS system late Sunday after Saudi Arabia, Venezuela and Mexico announced agreement to cut world oil output. \par \par \uc2  0318 GMT - *Dollar extended its gains against the yen by midday in Tokyo on Monday due to strong bids from interbank operators and commercial buying, but its topside was blocked near a technical resistance at about 131 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar's undertone stayed bullish, while speculation Japan might not be able to come up with a bold enough stimulus package continued to keep the yen under pressure, dealers aid. *Commercial demand and bids from investment trusts aiming to set up fresh investment trust funds provided a firm footing to the dollar/yen rate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *They said such demand from investment trusts was expected to continue until the end of March. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3n08x3k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
