\par\par \b \uc2  Headlines: Moody's Cuts Indonesia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Bond, Note Ceilings \b0\par\par\uc2 625 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 06:00\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Moody's downgraded the foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  country\par ceiling for bonds and notes of Indonesia to B3 from B2 and\par the foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ceiling for bank deposits to Ca from\par Caa1, citing concern over the country's deteriorating\par liquidity position [31819].\par    -- The IMF is still assessing Indonesia's prospects for\par workable economic reforms, although a key focus of its\par ongoing mission is the restoration of monetary policy control\par and discipline, according to officials [4403].\par    -- International rating agency Fitch IBCA cut the ratings\par on four leading Malaysian banks citing a deterioration in\par their operating environment this year [31811].\par    -- Japan's Securities and Exchange Surveillance\par Commission accused Yamaichi Securities and three former\par officials of the failed brokerage of hiding losses and\par transferring accounts to a paper company, sources close to\par the investigation said [31745].\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Sakakibara, vice minister for international affairs at\par Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said Japan is very concerned\par about the weakness of the yen, and the authorities are\par prepared to take steps to combat the yen's fall [31609].\par    -- The dollar plunged below Y131.00 and Y130.00 on rumors\par that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell dollars The\par dollar has since recovered some and is at Y130.10 from\par Y130.69 in New York late Thursday [4162].\par    -- Incoming Bank of Japan Governor Hayami said the recent\par weakening of the yen is temporary [4410].\par    -- U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Summers underlined the\par urgent need for aggressive fiscal stimulus by Japan [4232].\par    -- Japan should make its own decision in judging what\par kind of steps to take to boost its economy, finance minister\par Matsunaga replied [4405].\par    -- The head of Japan's Economic Planning Agency Omi said\par the content and timing of the government's next package to\par stimulate economic growth hasn't been decided [4409].\par    -- Japan's Minister of International Trade and Industry\par Horiuchi said the government's planned economic stimulus\par package should include a full-fledged income tax reform,\par rather than a one-time tax cut aimed at boosting demand\par temporarily [4441].\par    --Japan's lower house is set to approve the budget for\par the next fiscal year starting April 1 in its plenary session\par Friday, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported [4434].\par    -- Yakult Honsha said it has trading losses of Y105\par billion due to derivative and other financial dealings\par long-term debt ratings for the company on review for possible\par downgrade [31777].\par    -- The Indonesian economy is on the brink of\par hyperinflation and the government is committing significant\par breaches of its reform agreement with the IMF, according to a\par Australian Department of Foreign Affairs Report [31651].\par    -- President Suharto will eventually adopt a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par board plan to fix the Indonesian rupiah to the dollar, the\par leading proponent of the proposal said in an interview with\par the International Herald Tribune [31798].\par    -- The U.S. CPI edged up 0.1% in February, while the core\par CPI rose 0.3%, the Labor Department said [4017].\par    -- The seasonally adjusted U.S. goods and services trade\par deficit widened to $12.04 billion in January from December,\par the widest in more than a decade amid the Asian financial\par crisis, Commerce said [4015].\par    -- U.S. Treasurys are narrowly mixed in Tokyo, with the\par long bond down 5/32 at 103 to yield 5.91% [4041]. Debt\par futures ended lower at the CBOT Thursday, with the March bond\par at 120-25, down 1/32 [4101]. Japanese bonds are weaker\par    -- Stocks in Tokyo are mixed, with the Nikkei up 23.28 at\par 16,702.30 [4159]. Stocks ended higher in New York with the\par DJIA up about 27.65 points for the fourth record in a row\par    -- Gold is quoted at $292.25/oz in Hong Kong, compared\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  03-20-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0000EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4183 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du3k00piq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
