\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Crisis At A Glance:Dlr Dn Vs Yen On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rumor \b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 13:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  -- Eisuke Sakakibara, vice minister for international affairs at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Japan is very concerned about the weakness of the yen, and the authorities are prepared to take steps to combat the yen's fall [R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --The dollar dropped from a two-month high of Y132.23 after rumors that Japan's monetary authorities defended the yen. U.S. hedge funds had bought dollars on sentiment that Japan's next stimulus package may not be enough to jump-start the flagging economy. At 1230 GMT, the dollar was at Y129.95, down from Y130.69 late Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  --Japan MITI's Horiuchi said the government's planned stimulus package should include income tax reform, rather than a one-time tax cut. EPA head Omi said the content and timing of the package are undecided. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --The dollar shot below IDR10,000 after Indonesian Finance Minister Fuad said he expected to reach agreement with the International Monetary Fund next week, and confirmed that a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board is not feasible for now. At 0830 GMT, the rupiah was trading at IDR9,550 to the dollar. [*R/IO] \par \par \uc2  --Moody's cut the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ceiling for Indonesia's bonds and notes to B3 from B2, citing concern over the country's deteriorating liquidity position. In a related move, Moody's cut the ratings of 13 Indonesian banks to E, indicating the banks' existing or impending insolvency and need for outside support. [*R/IO] \par \par \uc2  --South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea denied a local newspaper report that South Korea and the IMF conditionally agreed to a lowering of local interest rates. The report helped Korean shares to close nearly 1% higher. [*R/SK] \par \par \uc2  --South Korea's 510 listed companies reported aggregate losses of KRW4.55 trillion in 1997, the Korea Stock Exchange reported. [*R/SK] \par \par \uc2  --Indonesian Vice President Habibie requested that Japanese bankers freeze principal and interest payments for one year on their short-term lending to Indonesian companies, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported. [*R/IO] \par \par \uc2  -- The IMF approved Indonesia's policy to subsidize essential food and medicines, but the subsidies are to be cut gradually in line with the exchange rate movement, the chairman of the State Logistics Agency said. Finance Minister Fuad has urged the IMF to drop its demands that Indonesia abolish the agency's monopoly control over the importation of staple foods, the Indonesian Observer reported. [*R/IO] \par \par \uc2  --Japanese soft-drink maker Yakult Honsha reported trading losses of Y105 billion due to derivative and other financial dealings, and said it will cut 300 staff. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  --Fitch IBCA cut the ratings on four big Malaysian banks, citing a deterioration in their operating environment since the beginning of the year. [*R/MY] \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par               Stock Index                       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                          Change      Level     Friday   Thursday\par Hong Kong  Hang Seng     Up 119.09  11,564.23 HK$7.7490 HK$7.7488\par Indonesisa Jakarta Comp  Up  12.581  516.731  IDR9,500  IDR10,270\par Japan      Nikkei        Up 151.45 16,830.47  Y129.95   Y130.69\par S. Korea   Kospi         Up  4.22   525.95   KRW1,448 KRW1,474\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-03-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1230GMT