\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr capped by BOJ sales but well-bid by late Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 680 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0649 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     130.11/21\tab \tab 131.30-128.95\par  USD/DEM     1.8324/34\tab \tab 1.8335-1.8278\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, March 20 (Reuters) - The dollar was capped against \par \par \uc2  the yen by late Tokyo on Friday, following the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  (BOJ) dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning, but strong \par \par \uc2  bids on falls lifted it off the day's low, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Late rounds of short-covering lifted the greenback \par \par \uc2  decisively above 130 yen after Moody's Investors Service \par \par \uc2  announced it had downgraded credit ratings of Japanese banks. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged more than two yen from its high to as low as 128.95 yen at one point in the morning after the BOJ sold dollars through the electronic broking system. \par \par \uc2  In an unusual move, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have avoided using major commercial banks for its dollar sales and instead asked a few smaller banks to handle them. \par \par \uc2  But at the lows, Japanese institutional investors scrambled for dollars aggressively against the yen. Japanese investment trusts, who bought dollars to set up fresh investment trust funds, were detected along with life insurers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said further short-covering led by overseas operators emerged by late trade to push the dollar above 130 yen after the announcement by Moody's. \par \par \uc2  Moody's said it has cut its financial strength rating for Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan Ltd (LTCB)  to E from E+. Moody's also said it has cut LTCB's long-term deposit rating to Baa2 from Baa1. \par \par \uc2  The rating agency also said it has put the Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd's  (IBJ) ratings under review with negative implications. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar could have gone well above 131 yen if the BOJ hadn't stepped in today. But the market has also confirmed the solidness of the dollar," a senior foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said bids aimed at setting investment trust funds are expected to emerge several times until the end of the Japanese fiscal book closings on March 31, which could be a key factor to provide firm support to the dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  In early trade, the dollar climbed to its high of 131.30 yen, triggered by remarks from newly appointed BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami, who was quoted by Jiji News Agency as saying on Friday there was no point in fretting over every \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  move. \par \par \uc2  "There would be no limit if one tried to worry about every move," Jiji quoted Hayami as saying. "It's important to watch the overall trend and it is necessary to closely monitor (the situation)." \par \par \uc2  The yen had been under selling pressure in New York on reports that Japanese health food company Yakult Honsha Co Ltd had incurred heavy losses through derivatives trading. \par \par \uc2  Yakult confirmed on Friday that it had lost 105.7 billion yen ($813 million) on derivatives and other asset management transactions. \par \par \uc2  A company executive told reporters that 64.7 billion yen of the losses came from derivatives trade, mostly on Nikkei share index swaps and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to carry over its bullish undertone against the yen, but caution over the BOJ action should limit aggressive buying. The market's focus will be on the Japanese ruling Liberal Democratic Party's outline for an economic stimulus plan. \par \par \uc2  Japanese media reported on Friday that the party will announce the package as early as next Wednesday, but the government will not flesh out the package until April. \par \par \uc2  Newly appointed BOJ Governor Hayami told reporters late on Friday that he will seek stability of the yen and the Japanese financial system. He also said the BOJ's monetary policy should be independent from politicians. The dollar reacted little to his comments so far. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 130.70/80 yen and 1.8230/25 marks in late New York on Thursday. ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3k08yq0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
