\par\par \b \uc2  Yen Cross - Yen off earlier highs versus Europeans. \b0\par\par\uc2 461 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 20 (Reuters) - The yen was off its earlier highs against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday afternoon in Tokyo cross trade. \par \par \uc2  The yen gained across the board earlier after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said bargain-hunting interest from Japanese institutional investors helped trim the yen's gains. \par \par \uc2  "Investors were keen to bargain hunt not only the dollar but also the mark and sterling for foreign securities investment," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  "With no attractive places to invest at home, Japanese investments in foreign bonds could pick up once the new fiscal year starts (on April 1)." \par \par \uc2  The mark stood around 71.07/10 yen as of 0535 GMT, compared with around 71.36 yen on late Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at 216.45/57 yen, versus around 217.96 yen in New York. \par \par \uc2  "Profit-taking activity (to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) by Japanese investors ahead of the March fiscal year-end seems to be largely over," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the mark will fall below 70 yen." \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar tumbled more than two yen from the day's high after the BOJ sold dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have sold dollars through a combination of an electronic broking system and conventional brokers. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ also appeared to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a few smaller banks. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Swiss franc stood at 87.01/06 yen, compared with around 87.38 yen in New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar was at 86.13/23 yen, compared with 86.27/37 yen earlier. \par \par \uc2  Although the sentiment towards the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained bearish, the market was cautious due to fears the BOJ might step in again to support the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Most people seem to agree that the yen's downtrend will not be reversed without a dramatic loosening of the Japanese government's tight fiscal policy," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "But fears of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will certainly help slow the dollar's rise." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) will announce the outline of an economic stimulus plan as early as next Wednesday, but the government will not flesh out the package until April, Japanese media reported on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said any economic package would be ineffective without fresh income tax cuts. \par \par \uc2  But Taku Yamasaki, the LDP's chief policy-maker, told Reuters in an interview on Wednesday that income tax cuts are unlikely to be included in the upcoming economic stimulus package. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3k08ul1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
