\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: Option-Related Selling Around Y131.00 \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 07:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dollar could well go as high as Y134.00 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  commit to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the yen, market participants said. For one thing, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now might not have the desired effect. \par \par \uc2  'If there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels, we'd buy the dollar back up,' the U.K, bank trader said. 'There's no reason to buy the yen.' \par \par \uc2  As a result, the announcement early in the day that Japan's February trade surplus grew more than expected had little impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, traders said. Japan's merchandise trade surplus rose 88.7% to Y1.285 trillion from the year before, while its politically sensitive trade surplus with the U.S. rose 32.9% to Y539.0 billion. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar faces short-term resistance around Y130.50-60, where it topped out Wednesday. Tokyo players said the dollar might make a try for Y131.00 in overseas trading later in the day, but that ahead of the March 31 fiscal year end in Japan, many participants seemed content to stay on the sidelines for the short term. \par \par \uc2  'Given the dollar's sharp rise Wednesday, profit-taking at this level is only natural,' Nippon Credit Bank's Shiori said. 'In addition, there's a lot of defensive option-related selling around Y131.00, just as there was around Y130.00.' \par \par \uc2  The dollar managed to rise against the mark after the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  succumed to some profit-taking selling of marks for yen. But traders said the mark should resume its rise up against its Japanese counterpart. \par \par \uc2  'The mark fell through support at Y71.30, but it should recover that level and make a move up to Y72.00,' the U.K. bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at Y71.17, down from Y71.21 in New York late Wednesday and below Y71.27 in London late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6692, down from $1.6718 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6705 in London late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0618GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917du3j02g28\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
