\par\par \b \uc2  Japan govt moves could snag dollar's rise-traders. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tatsuo Ito \par \uc2 668 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 09:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 13 (Reuters) - The dollar is expected to continue a bull run against the yen but downside risks exist because of government efforts to lift the stock market and the yen towards the end of March, senior traders said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  An unprecedented scandal this week involving the Bank of Japan and the generally poor condition of Japan's economy accelerated dollar-buying, but political efforts just before corporate book-closings on March 31 may be a pitfall for the rise of the dollar, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is inclined to head higher towards 130 yen, but there would be a battle (against government efforts to stem such a rise)," said Nao Nakajima, vice president and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Bank of America in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The government and monetary authorities are expected to step up efforts to boost the Nikkei Stock Average to the key 18,000 level at the end of March, while restraining the yen from weakening to more than 130 yen per dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Asahi Shimbun newspaper reported the government will include use of 1.3 trillion yen in public funds from postal savings (Yucho) and insurance funds (Kampo) to boost share prices in an economic package to be unveiled on March 20, although Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga said on Friday he had not officially heard of that idea. \par \par \uc2  But the benchmark 225-share Nikkei average was buoyed by the report, ending up 484.92 points at 17,060.14 on Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official Haruhiko Kuroda said on Thursday that the dollar's overnight push above 129.00 yen was excessive and the ministry was prepared to act if necessary. \par \par \uc2  There was market talk that Japanese public fund bodies were placing offers above 129.00 yen on Thursday, which raised speculation they were trying to cap the dollar's rise on behalf of Japan's monetary authorities, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "(The monetary authorities) may want the yen to strengthen to at least 125 per dollar by the end of March," said Masanori Mizoguchi general manager of securities investment department at Nippon Dantai Life Insurance Co Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said if the yen weakens to 130 per dollar at the end of March it may prompt sales of Japanese stock holdings by foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  Japanese banks would also face problems because their foreign assets would be inflated by a weak yen and this would reduce their capital ratios. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's weakening to above 130 would be troublesome simply because it would reduce our capital ratio," said a spokesman at a leading Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to around 129.70 yen overseas on Thursday. It stood at 128.50 yen late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Some traders also speculated that the outcome of Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto's trip to Jakarta on Saturday and Sunday may lead to yen buying next week if the Japanese government comes up with any surprises to help regain confidence in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  This is despite views that Hashimoto's visit alone cannot produce a breakthrough in a standoff between the IMF and Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Influential Finance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara will join Hashimoto in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (for yen) may be possible, taking the yen's relationship with Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into account," said Koichiro Amaya, vice president at JP Morgan. \par \par \uc2  Amaya said if Japanese monetary authorities see the current yen weakness leading to falls of some Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be justified. \par \par \uc2  "In addition, there is a desire among Japanese monetary authorities to correct the yen's current weakness because it has primarily been fuelled by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's internal problems," he said. \par \par \uc2  "However, whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have an effect is a different question," Amaya said. \par \par \uc2  He said it might be difficult to carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effectively amid a lack of economic policies that would back up that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-1396 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du3d0039e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
