\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday -2: Verbal  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  From  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 03:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Renewed dollar strength against the yen is heightening concern in the market that Japanese monetary authorities will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lend a helping hand to the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  This concern was heightened by comments earlier Thursday by a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official. Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the ministry's international finance bureau said, 'The yen is excessively weak,' and added that the ministry is 'ready to take decisive steps to stop a fall in the yen.' \par \par \uc2  The market continues to keep an eye on Japanese stocks for cues on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. Further weakness will likely bode well for the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei stock index ended the morning session down 31.76 points at 16,724.38. \par \par \uc2  'Overall dollar strength is helped by weakness in Japanese stocks,' said a trader at a foreign bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, Japan's Economic Planning Agency (EPA) is scheduled to release January data on core machinery orders at 0500 GMT Thursday. Core machinery orders to Japanese manufacturers in January, after adjustment for seasonal factors, are expected to have risen 4.8% from the previous month, according to a survey of economists by Nikkei-Dow Jones. \par \par \uc2  The mark is at Y70.49, up from Y70.45 earlier in Tokyo but below Y70.65 in New York late Wednesday. The mark was quoted in Tokyo late Wednesday at Y69.88. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6474, flat from $1.6475 earlier in Tokyo but below $1.6487 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6405 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar is seen trading between Y128.50-Y129.60 and\par DM1.8280-DM1.8350 for the rest of the Asian day.\par By Arran Scott 813-5255-2984; amscott@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-03-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0254GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3c025kl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
