\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar ends U.S. down, profit-taking erases gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, March 11 (Reuters) - The dollar ended New York trading lower on Wednesday as profit-taking chipped away at strong gains amassed as a bribery scandal widened in Japan and German rates were expected to be held steady. \par \par \uc2  "We have seen profit-taking as well some selling from some central banks near the top levels for the dollar," a dealer said, adding however the late session retreat should not extinguish the dollar's generally firm tone. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen, which roared to a seven-week high as the Nikkei index fell 1.3 percent on news a bribery scandal had engulfed the Bank of Japan, ended at 129.35/45 from its 129.50/60 open. \par \par \uc2  Against the mark, the dollar slipped to 1.8305/10 from its 1.8366/69 opening level. \par \par \uc2  Prosecutors raided the Bank of Japan and arrested Yasuyuki Yoshizawa, the head of the bank's capital markets division, who allegedly leaked advance information about the bank's top-secret daily money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In return he was allegedly treated to golf outings and lavish entertainment. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the arrest signaled the scandal, which prompted Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka's resignation in January, might also force Bank of Japan governor Yasuo Matsushita to step down. \par \par \uc2  "The arrest and talk that Matsushita may have to resign is not a yen supportive factor," explained Bob Lynch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas, adding however that dollar gains would be limited before Japan's March 31 fiscal-year end. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there had been talk that an Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been interested in selling dollar/yen to protect a knockout option at 130 yen, and several also mentioned nervousness about possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around those levels. \par \par \uc2  "There is some hesitation to probe much above 130 at the moment simply because of the uncertainty involving some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  While traders worried about the scandal's immediate impact on the yen, several said it would eventually support the yen. \par \par \uc2  "Ultimately there will be some benefits for the yen," said David Gilmore, partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics. \par \par \uc2  Profit-taking also erased the dollar's gains against the mark which were triggered after the Bundesbank released a study suggesting Germany's real inflation rate is well below that shown in official consumer price statistics. Later news that German inflation slowed to 1.1 percent in February helped support sentiment the Bundesbank would not raise rates soon. \par \par \uc2  But rekindled talk of a UK rate hike boosted sterling. \par \par \uc2  In dealings against the yen, traders said the market was still being swayed between wanting to buy the dollar as a safe-haven asset and selling it amid talk that Japan is taking serious steps in overhauling its economic system. \par \par \uc2  "There is a lot of uncertainty, and basically the big investors are sidelined waiting for stops to be hit at higher levels before coming back in," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  News that Japan Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto vowed to investigate allegations that senior officials at the finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had accepted lavish meals for leaking information was a welcome sign the system may be overhauled. \par \par \uc2  Extending its gains against the mark, sterling was poised for a possible test of 3.03 marks, dealers said, adding however that gains would only last as long as the market believed the Bank of England will raise rates. \par \par \uc2  "Strength is going to erode as soon as they do it because then the cycle of rate hikes will be over," Gilmore said. \par \par \uc2  The pound climbed to $1.6479/89 from $1.6402/12. The dollar fell against the Swiss franc to 1.4900/10 from 1.4941/51 and was mostly unchanged at C$1.4073/78 from C$1.4072/77. The Australian dollar stood at $0.6660/65 versus $0.6661/66. \par \par \uc2  ((-Svea Herbst-Bayliss, NA Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du3b007vr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
