\par\par \b \uc2  Asia hopes G7 cavalry will try riding to the rescue. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Phil Smith \par \uc2 828 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1998\par 08:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Feb 20 (Reuters) - Floundering Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  clutched at the straw of G7 help ahead of a meeting of the top industrialised countries in London this weekend. \par \par \uc2  The excitement began after an article in Japan's Nihon Keizai Shimbun, which did not cite any sources, said the Group of Seven meeting would discuss concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The expectation is the communique will contain an expression of "close cooperation for the stability of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", the paper said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders and analysts also reckon the communique may contain a rupiah-stabilising alternative to Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board idea for a fixed exchange rate system. \par \par \uc2  The controversial \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board plan has raised hackles at the IMF, and officials from countries involved in the $43 billion bail-out package which the fund orchestrated for Indonesia have said it is not a good idea at the moment. \par \par \uc2  IMF chief Michel Camdessus has even threatened not to hand over any more cash if the scheme goes ahead and on Friday an IMF official said such a scheme was "premature". \par \par \uc2  But it is not just the economic crisis in Indonesia that is worrying G7 countries. Security concerns are also being voiced by the United States and Australia. \par \par \uc2  Riots over food prices have erupted across the world's fourth most populous nation and with hyper-inflation looming due to the rupiah's 70 percent drop in value since last July, things can only get worse, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Unrest in the mid-1960s shook the country as it was mired in the depths of poverty. An abortive communist coup bid in 1965 was followed by an anti-communist pogrom in which 500,000 people are estimated to have died. \par \par \uc2  "I worry about the potential for internal trouble. I worry about the potential for social disorder...," Australian Prime Minister John Howard said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The possible collapse of Asian markets in general is something that will concern G7, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The region absorbs a sizeable chunk of exports from the industrialised nations and if the West allows Asia to stew, it would be like standing idly by while a good customer dies on the steps of your shop. \par \par \uc2  "The Asia crisis is something G7 cannot ignore," said Chiang Yao Chye, head of Asia Pacific Research at CIBC in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "I think they will try and do something and the U.S. has already indicated some kind of credit facility on the export side. But whether they provide any concrete \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets remains to be seen." \par \par \uc2  While analysts said it certainly would not take much to give them a boost, few believed that actual cash \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by any of the G7, except maybe \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was in the offing. \par \par \uc2  "It would in fact be quite cheap for G7 to get these regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "They wouldn't have to come in in size given all these markets are so thin and tiny compared to the majors. Getting dollar/yen going is one thing, but this is quite another, it really wouldn't cost them much at all. But all that said, I don't really see it. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. (authorities) are running in to trouble over cash already committed to Asia. I don't see actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an option," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer was referring to protests by the U.S. public over funds already sent to Asia and some officials saying the Clinton administration should sort out problems at home first. \par \par \uc2  The other argument against actual cash \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the fact that many corporates and individuals in Asia are still dollar hungry and would absorb any that G7 central banks threw at the market. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin appeared to pour cold water on the idea of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday by declining to comment on the possibility of G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I never discussed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Rubin's remarks triggered a round of dollar short-covering against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The rupiah was weaker at 9,000/9150 at 0612 GMT compared to around 8,600 at the close on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit was also lower on Rubin's comments, trading at 3.7600/7900 at 0610 GMT compared to 3.7400/7700 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, some G7 agreement on trade financing and technical assistance was quite likely, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "It would only take a little to get the momentum going, then the market would take over," CIBC's Chiang said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the only G7 nation to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the crisis, alongside the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) on the rupiah late last year. \par \par \uc2  Analysts noted that Germany now seems to be taking a more active role following a visit to Indonesia, South Korea and Thailand by Finance Minister Theo Waigel this week. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du2k01hi4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
