\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo-2: Ex-MOF Utsumi Hints At  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Over Y130 \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1998\par 02:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark is trading at Y72.54, up from Y72.39 earlier and above Y72.16 in New York late Wednesday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Wednesday at Y72.69. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6245, up from $1.6237 earlier but below $1.6256 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6219 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Additionally, Makoto Utsumi, formerly vice minister for international affairs at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said it's 'natural' for monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets as a means of sending a signal that the dollar's rise into the Y130 level represents excessive yen weakness, the Nikkei reported. \par \par \uc2  He also said that a desirable level for the dollar was between Y110 and Y120 and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to fall toward that level by year-end. \par \par \uc2  While tax cuts or other fiscal stimulus measures might be a condition for the U.S. to join \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen, senior government officials said Wednesday were cold to more cuts. \par \par \uc2  Chief Cabinet spokesman Kanezo Muraoka said he didn't know how such tax cuts could be financed, while Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said the government has already taken sufficient steps for now. \par \par \uc2  The comments came after a newly formed alliance of six Japanese opposition parties advanced a proposal for an additional Y6 trillion in tax cuts. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said that the market would be watching the movement of Tokyo stocks and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which if lower would weigh on the yen. \par \par \uc2  'While South Korea has stabilized somewhat, we'll have to watch the situation in Indonesia, China and Hong Kong closely,' said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei stock index average is up 450.95 points to 15,479.12 at 0115 GMT. \par \par \uc2  -By James Simms, 81-3-5255-2940; jsimms@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0140GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1800502\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
