\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/yen firmer in Europe,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  nerves wane. \b0\par\par\uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 8 (Reuters) - The dollar edged higher from overnight lows against the mark and yen as market worries of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop the yen waned and ongoing nervousness over Asia's financial health. \par \par \uc2  Japan Vice Finance Minister Eisuke Sakakibara said after meetings with U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers and Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Wednesday that the U.S. and Japan would continue to cooperate on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But there was no news on joint action to stem yen falls and a Washington Post article said today the U.S. would be reluctant to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until it saw steps from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost its economy. \par \par \uc2  "Yesterday the market tended to close dollar longs ahead of the Sakakibara and Summers meeting so the market is not so overbought as it was on Tuesday," said Klaus Kusber, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  "With no comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market is in a situation where it could gain momentum to push dollar/yen higher." \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen climbed steadily from an overnight low of 131.30 yen to trade at 133.10/20 by morning Europe. It stood at 131.75/85 yen late Wednesday in Europe. Mark/yen also recovered from overnight lows below 72 to trade at 72.68/71 this morning. \par \par \uc2  The weak Asia picture was kept in focus with a collapse in the Indonesian rupiah which sunk close to a major psychological level of 10,000 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Doubts over the Indonesia government's ability to overcome its financial crisis and growing concerns it will default on it foreign debt have kept the Asia turmoil simmering despite the steadier performance of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said today it could not consider further income tax cuts, denting earlier speculation Japan would take more steps to boost its economy. This lifted the yen and Nikkei overnight but those gains were eroded by the Asia close. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/yen is going to be bought on dips for now, but it won't be easy for it to get up to the 135 yen target soon," said Jesper Dannesboe, treasury economist at ABN-Amro in London. \par \par \uc2  "As the focus on dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  intensifies, the market will turn to other yen crosses and we should see more mark/yen buying emerging." \par \par \uc2  Mark/yen has kept in a broad sideways range since mid-November but given the weak Asia backdrop, analysts said an upside break is only a matter of time. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark shrugged off mark/yen's early gains, trading at 1.8305/12 marks at 0935 GMT from 1.8230/35 marks late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Market attention is on today's regular Bundesbank council meeting though few expect any change in German interest rates. The Bank of England's monetary policy committee also makes its announcement on UK interest rates today, expected at 1200 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Eyes are also on today's U.S. producer price data for December at 1330 GMT. Headline prices are seen dipping 0.3 percent on the month and core data down 0.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  But the big data prize this week remains Friday's U.S. and German employment data for December. \par \par \uc2  ((Andrew Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com))