\par\par \b \uc2  =Asia Crisis/Glance: Dlr Down On Fears Of Joint  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par 17:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will discuss with the U.S. the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets later this week, according to an international monetary source traveling with a delegation of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials. \par \par \uc2  -- The dollar is lower against the yen at mid-morning Wednesday, dropping to 131.91 yen, down from 133.63 late Tuesday in New York, as concerns intensified that the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may discuss the possibility of joint dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar had risen to a 5-1/2-year high of 134.40 yen in Asian trading, before the news of the possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talks hit the market. \par \par \uc2  -- The Malaysian ringgit rebounded 7% against the dollar from its intraday low in Asian trading Wednesday after Malaysia's deputy prime minister said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 'grossly undervalued.' However, the dollar ended Asia trading at MYR4.5755, up from 4.3400 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  -- Japanese and U.S. officials will focus much of their discussion on the situation in Asian financial markets when they meet in Washington, Minister of Finance Mitsuzuka said. \par \par \uc2  -- House Banking Committee Chairman James Leach is scheduled to depart Jan. 15 for a three-nation fact-finding tour of Asia. The tour is designed partly to address questions over the IMF's role in fighting financial-market crises. \par \par \uc2  -- Hong Kong shares dropped Wednesday, closing down almost 6% on Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters, and fears of a Hong Kong interest rate rise. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  07-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1625GMT \par \par \uc2  4190 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010914du17005ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
