\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Yen Volatilities Ease After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par 08:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Volatilities implied by Japanese yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options eased a bit in Tokyo Tuesday compared with their levels in New York late Monday, as the dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  put a brake on the dollar's one-way rise. \par \par \uc2  In the Tuesday Asian morning session, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to Y134.30 - a 67-month high against the yen - before the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the dollar's further rise. \par \par \uc2  Although the market still remains bullish about the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was hemmed in below the Y134.00-level for the rest of the session. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar's rise was temporarily checked. That made traders less active in dollar-yen option trading,' said a trader at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  As a result, one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options in the over-the-counter market imply volatility of 14.9% bid, slightly down from 14.95% in New York Monday, but above 14.2% in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  However, market participants expect the volatility to rise above 15%-bid soon. 'The dollar is unlikely to stop (rising) here. As it resumes, volatilities will further go up,' said another Japanese city bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Deutsche mark volatilities are higher at 11.45% from 11.4% in New York Monday. Dollar/mark options were quoted at 10.4% in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 0700 GMT (2 a.m. EST), the dollar is at Y133.50 and DM1.8285, mixed from Y133.58 and DM1.8250 late Monday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Risk-reversals favor dollar call options against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either put or call options by the premium or discount applied. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0742GMT \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du16002co\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
