\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fails To Support Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Takeshi Takeuchi \par \uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par 06:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  barely succeeded in propping up the yen amid continuing strong dollar-bullish sentiment, leaving the dollar slightly higher against the yen Tuesday than its levels in New York late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit also edged higher against the Deutsche mark, helped by the rise of the dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Following the quick rise of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen Monday in European and U.S. markets, the dollar continued to rise early, hitting Y134.30 at 0046 GMT (7:46 p.m. EST), its highest level since April 27, 1992, when it touched Y134.95. \par \par \uc2  'The continuing malaise of (Japan's) stock market and lingering pessimism over the Japanese economy naturally accelerate the dollar-buying binge,' said Koichi Kubo, assistant manger of international \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  group at Dai-ichi Kangyo Bank. \par \par \uc2  However, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around Y134.00 to rein in the dollar, pushing the unit down to Y133.10 before it bounced back again. \par \par \uc2  Expected further BOJ dollar selling in the near term, however, 'is unlikely to be effective in the long run,' said Kubo. 'The fundamentals of the U.S. economy is so strong that no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can stop the dollar's rise.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0525 GMT (12:25 a.m. EST), the dollar is quoted at Y133.65, above Y133.58 late Monday in New York, but down from Y134.00 late Monday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at DM1.8293, higher than DM1.8250 late Monday in New York and above DM1.8255 in London Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 06-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0539GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du160023n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
