\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Knocks Dollar Lower \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par 03:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  knocked the dollar off its highest level versus the yen since April 1992, but the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered partially on buying by U.S. funds and Japanese institutional investors who were waiting in the wings to take advantage of dollar dips. \par \par \uc2  At midday in Tokyo, the dollar was mixed compared with its levels earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to an intraday high of Y134.30 at 0046 GMT, its highest level since touching Y134.95 on April 27, 1992. But BOJ dollar selling pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down to around Y133.10 before the dollar bounced back. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese monetary official, speaking with Dow Jones on condition of anonymity, confirmed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars, although he declined to provide other details of the action. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the BOJ selling provided market participants with an opportunity to buy more dollars. \par \par \uc2  'They're waiting for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy,' said Shinji Imanishi, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Sumitomo Trust and Banking, adding that the dollar is likely to see volatile movements between Y132.50 to Y134.50 for the rest of the session. \par \par \uc2  Around 0215 GMT (9:15 p.m. EST), the dollar is trading at Y133.75, slightly down from Y134.02 around 0055 GMT (7:55 p.m. EST) and above Y133.58 in New York late Monday. The dollar was quoted at Y132.05 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DM1.8325, higher than DM1.8290 earlier in Tokyo and above DM1.8250 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at DM1.7970 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 06-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0228GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du16001tu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
