\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr spurns BOJ, stays well-supported by late Tokyo. [CORRECTED 07:50 GMT] \b0\par\par\uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 6 (Reuters) - The dollar fell off from early highs against the yen but was well-supported by late Tokyo trade as bargain-hunters bid up the greenback despite morning \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Persistent weakness in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sound economic fundamentals in the United States continued to make the dollar the most attractive choice among investors, they said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dipped near 133 yen and 1.83 marks amid corrective selling (corrects from "amid short covering"), but many operators were willing to bid up the greenback, especially against the Japanese unit. \par \par \uc2  "There is ample demand on falls," said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. "Bids keep on emerging against the yen." \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can slow the dollar's momentum, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be unable to change the market's basic sentiment, he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to 134.38 yen -- its highest level since April 1992 -- in morning trade, but the BOJ's sales knocked it down below 133 yen. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to have stepped in to sell dollars at around 134.20 yen. It later sold the greenback intermittently below 134 yen in the morning, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the dollar to defend the yen on December 19. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the dollar, but created a great buying opportunity for bargain-hunters. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ's sales came at around the local fixing when there was huge commercial buying demand," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have worked more effectively had it chosen more appropriate timing." \par \par \uc2  Traders ignored morning comments by Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka, who expressed concern about the yen's weakness. \par \par \uc2  "There is no doubt that we are worried," he told a news conference. "Excessive weakness of the yen is not favourable." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said fears of possible concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the United States, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other Group of Seven (G7) countries have waned somewhat following overnight comments by U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin. \par \par \uc2  On Monday in New York, Rubin reiterated that a strong dollar was in the best interests of the United States. \par \par \uc2  "Speculative dollar buying seems to have intensified this morning after Rubin's comments," the U.S. bank dealer said. But given the dollar's bullishness, the possibility of a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot be ruled out, he said. \par \par \uc2  Asia's lingering financial woes also kept the dollar well-bid. Although some Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered from their lows by late in the day, they were still under strong speculative selling pressure, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  As of 0740 GMT, the Indonesian rupiah recovered to 7,200/7,350 to the dollar after falling to a record low of 7,700 in the morning. It opened at 7,000/7,200. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht stood at 51.80 to the dollar in the onshore market, after diving to 52.00 earlier. It was at 50.00/50.20 late on Monday. It fell as low as 54.40 in the offshore market from 49.85/50.35 in late trading. ((-- Tokyo Treasury Desk (813) 3432-8785 email: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du160167o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
